## \'a78 \'97 Operational Principles\
\
### 8.1 The Asymmetry Correction\
\
The fundamental insight of the ADJR protocol is that **justice is not symmetric.** A state can file a thousand lawsuits for the cost of a clerk's salary. A human being defending against a single lawsuit may lose their home, their career, their health, and their family. Any system that treats the filer and the target as equal participants in a "neutral" process is not neutral\'97it is structurally biased in favor of the entity with greater institutional throughput.\
\
The ADJR corrects this asymmetry not by weakening the state's ability to pursue legitimate claims, but by **imposing costs on the attack pattern itself.** Volume filing is rate-limited. Jurisdictional scattering is consolidated. Temporal delay is penalized. The attacker's institutional advantages are neutralized at the structural level, restoring the proceeding to a contest of *evidence and merit* rather than a war of *attrition and endurance.*\
\
### 8.2 The Living Defendant Principle\
\
No system of justice can claim legitimacy if it permits the prosecution of entities that cannot defend themselves. The dead cannot hire lawyers. The dead cannot testify. The dead cannot exercise the right to confront their accusers. A proceeding against a corpse is not a trial. It is a monologue delivered to an empty chair.\
\
The Dead Hand Prohibition exists not to protect the reputations of the dead\'97the dead have no reputations, only the memories of the living\'97but to **remove the incentive to produce corpses.** When a system allows posthumous conviction, it creates a rational economic strategy: *kill the target, then convict the body.* The DHP eliminates this strategy by voiding the conviction. The corpse is worthless as a legal target. Therefore, the target is more valuable alive.\
\
### 8.3 The Good Day Invariant\
\
A "good day" is defined as follows:\
\
```\
GOOD_DAY(entity) =\
  entity.alive = TRUE \uc0\u8743 \
  entity.counsel_accessible = TRUE \uc0\u8743 \
  entity.actions_against < RATE_LIMIT \uc0\u8743 \
  entity.oldest_pending < TEMPORAL_BOUND \uc0\u8743 \
  entity.enforcement_response \uc0\u8804  BASELINE_MEDIAN \u8743 \
  entity.liveness_beacon = CURRENT \uc0\u8743 \
  entity.shield \uc0\u8712  \{Inactive, Monitoring\} \u8743 \
  entity.posthumous_liability = ZERO \uc0\u8743 \
  entity.estate_new_claims = ZERO \uc0\u8743 \
  entity.freedom_to_conduct_work = UNIMPAIRED\
```\
\
**The purpose of the ADJR is to make good days structurally inevitable rather than accidentally possible.**\
